      </header>

      <div class="post-content">
        <p class="lead">
            Despite significant progress in machine learning, existing models often operate under a closed-world assumption, where test data are assumed to follow the same distribution as the training data. Out-of-distribution (OOD) detection, which aims to identify unexpected inputs from unknown classes, has emerged as a pivotal approach for enhancing the reliability of machine learning models. This tutorial presents a comprehensive overview of the theoretical foundations and cutting-edge techniques in OOD detection. We begin by introducing the tutorial goals, real-world motivations, and problem formulation. We then review traditional OOD detection methods, followed by an in-depth discussion of OOD detection with vision-language models and diffusion models. Finally, we identify open challenges and outline promising future research directions in OOD detection
            
        
        </p>


